<section id="outline-container-orgc8c1c5d" class="outline-2">
<h2 id="orgc8c1c5d">Troubleshooting</h2>
<div class="outline-text-2" id="text-orgc8c1c5d">
</div>
<div id="outline-container-orgae71c79" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="orgae71c79">"Cannot find csharp-ls" or Eglot won't start</h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-orgae71c79">
<ol class="org-ol">
<li>Check the PATH: <code>M-x getenv RET PATH</code></li>
<li>Verify the DLL exists at the configured location</li>
<li>Try running manually: <code>dotnet path\to\CSharpLanguageServer.dll --version</code></li>
<li>Check <code>*eglot-events*</code> buffer for detailed error messages</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="outline-container-orga512d27" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="orga512d27">LSP is slow or uses too much memory</h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-orga512d27">
<p>
Try adding to your configuration:
</p>

<div class="org-src-container">
<pre class="src src-emacs-lisp"><span style="color: #5B6268;">;; </span><span style="color: #5B6268;">Increase garbage collection threshold during LSP operations
</span>(<span style="color: #ea3d54; font-weight: bold;">setq</span> gc-cons-threshold 100000000)  <span style="color: #5B6268;">; </span><span style="color: #5B6268;">100MB
</span>(<span style="color: #ea3d54; font-weight: bold;">setq</span> read-process-output-max (* 1024 1024))  <span style="color: #5B6268;">; </span><span style="color: #5B6268;">1MB</span>
</pre>
</div><br>
</div>
</div>
<div id="outline-container-orgc4a1901" class="outline-3">
<h3 id="orgc4a1901">Debugger won't attach</h3>
<div class="outline-text-3" id="text-orgc4a1901">
<ol class="org-ol">
<li>Ensure the project is built in Debug configuration</li>
<li>Check the DLL path matches your build output</li>
<li>Look at <code>*dape-repl*</code> for error messages</li>
<li>Verify netcoredbg runs: <code>netcoredbg.exe --version</code></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="outline-container-orgafc5e3f" class="outline-2">
<h2 id="orgafc5e3f">Conclusion</h2>
<div class="outline-text-2" id="text-orgafc5e3f">
<p>
This setup has served me well for my windows .NET 9.0 projects and various other C# work. The key benefits:
</p>

<ul class="org-ul">
<li><b>Portability</b>: Everything lives in one directory</li>
<li><b>Speed</b>: csharp-ls is notably faster than OmniSharp</li>
